  "section_notes": "The final v36 text is strong on safety: 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, a 55 °C test with a 5% cap and immediate sales stop, a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition window, and a 36-month built-in suppression deadline. The Hearth 10 (6.2%) is blocked from new sales until it passes retest, and the Ember 8 (9.9) must be recalled, while the 6-year retrofit window for shut-off mainly benefits Northwind (38% coverage). Customers receive numerical per-model rates, but public publication is not required."
